            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>Q: How often should aerosol chain lubricant be reapplied?</strong><br>
                A: Reapplication depends on the environment. For industrial conveyors, a weekly schedule is common, whereas for high-speed motorcycles, every 500-800km is recommended.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Q: Can I use aerosol lubricants on O-ring chains?</strong><br>
                A: Yes, provided the formulation is "O-ring safe." You must avoid harsh aromatic solvents that can swell or degrade the rubber seals.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Q: Why is it important to wait after applying the lubricant?</strong><br>
                A: The "settling time" allows the carrier solvents to evaporate, leaving behind the high-adhesion film. Using the chain immediately can cause the lubricant to fling off.
            </p>

            <div class="author-section">
